ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":143,"prev":145,"next":148,"titles":151,"firmware":72},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":9,"order":10,"path":11,"context":12,"summary":18,"status":19,"firmware":20,"facts":27,"procedures":85,"parameters":100,"related":101,"body":104,"sources":105,"official_url":31,"controls":116},"sampler.multisampler","Multisampler",[5,6,7,8],"multisample","multi sampler","key zones","sampled instrument","sampler",50,"knowledge/manual/units/sampler/multisampler.md",{"modes":13,"screens":15},[14],"instrument",[16,17],"M1","sample","Up to 24 samples of one instrument, each on its own zone of the keyboard; a sample also plays the empty keys below it, and `M1` edits the selected zone like the synth sampler.","current",{"min":21,"changed_in":22,"guide_version":25,"verified_on":26},"1.0.9",[23,24],"1.1.0","1.1.25","1.1.15",null,[28,33,36,39,42,45,48,53,56,59,64,68,74,77,81],{"id":29,"text":30,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"what","Each range of notes plays from a recording made near its pitch, which sounds truer than stretching one sample.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/sample#multisampler","official",{"id":34,"text":35,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"zones","While recording, select keys from left to right; every key that gets a sample becomes a zone.",{"id":37,"text":38,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"fill-down","Zones fill downwards — a sample also covers the empty keys below it, pitched down, as far as the next zone.",{"id":40,"text":41,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"max","Up to 24 zones fit, about three samples per octave.",{"id":43,"text":44,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"record-keys","The record page works like the drum sampler's — press a key to choose the zone (it lights up), then `hold M1`; `M2` / `M3` step through filled keys, `M4` unassigns, and takes also go to the user folder.",{"id":46,"text":47,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"threshold","As on every record page, the take starts only once the input passes the threshold set with `E4`.",{"id":49,"text":50,"source":51,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":52},"root","The key you record on becomes the zone's top key and root (presets the unit writes set each zone's root to its top key), so play that key's note into the input.","docs/research/30-presets-samples.md#27-region-fields-by-type","derived",{"id":54,"text":55,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"editing","The multisampler's `M1` page has the synth sampler's layout, loop type included (`shift + click E3`).",{"id":57,"text":58,"source":51,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":52},"caption-mixup","The guide titles `shift + turn E2` and `shift + turn E3` pan and sample fade but describes tune and loop crossfade; zones store tune and crossfade, not pan.",{"id":60,"text":61,"source":62,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":63},"no-layers","There are no velocity layers or round robins — one sample per zone.","docs/research/30-presets-samples.md#32-counts-and-structure-limits","community",{"id":65,"text":66,"source":67,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"transpose","OS 1.1.25 improved how multisamples follow global transpose.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.25",{"id":69,"text":70,"source":71,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":72,"confidence":73},"screen","The top strip is a full keyboard on which the zone of the sample being played lights up, jumping with the octave; each zone brings its own waveform and markers, and the shift layer matches the synth sampler's.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#25-engine-pages-instrument-m1","1.1.33","verified",{"id":75,"text":76,"source":71,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":72,"confidence":73},"no-cc","CC12–15 on the track's channel move nothing on this page.",{"id":78,"text":79,"source":80,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":26,"confidence":52},"no-locks","OS 1.1.0 gave parameter locks to the drum and synth samplers and does not name the multisampler; the replica gives its zones none, which is not yet checked on a unit.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.0",{"id":82,"text":83,"source":84,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":63},"take-name","A multisampler take is named after its key's note in the same project-note-track.wav pattern as other takes (community, OS 1.x).","docs/research/78-overnight-accuracy.md#log",[86],{"id":87,"goal":88,"preconditions":89,"steps":91,"result":26,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"record-zones","Multisample an instrument",[90],"the track uses the multisampler",[92,94,97],{"keys":17,"note":93,"set":26},"set source, gain and threshold here (`turn E1`, `turn E3`, `turn E4`)",{"keys":95,"note":96,"set":26},"key","start low and work to the right; the key lights up",{"keys":98,"note":99,"set":26},"hold M1","play that key's note; the take starts once it passes the threshold. Repeat on the next key",[],[102,103],"sampler.synth-sampler","sampler.sampling","Sample the instrument every few notes and let the zones fill the gaps below each one.",[106,108,110,111,113,114,115],{"url":31,"kind":107},"guide",{"url":51,"kind":109},"research",{"url":62,"kind":109},{"url":67,"kind":112},"changelog",{"url":71,"kind":109},{"url":80,"kind":112},{"url":84,"kind":109},[117,118,119,120,121,122,123,124,125,126,127,128,129,130,131,132,133,134,135,136,137,138,139,140,141,142],"key.sample","keyboard.f3","keyboard.fs3","keyboard.g3","keyboard.gs3","keyboard.a3","keyboard.as3","keyboard.b3","keyboard.c4","keyboard.cs4","keyboard.d4","keyboard.ds4","keyboard.e4","keyboard.f4","keyboard.fs4","keyboard.g4","keyboard.gs4","keyboard.a4","keyboard.as4","keyboard.b4","keyboard.c5","keyboard.cs5","keyboard.d5","keyboard.ds5","keyboard.e5","key.m1",{"id":9,"title":144},"Sampler",{"id